common errors of k8s

Q.1 what causes pod crashloop backoff error?
 Kubectl logs podname
There might me few  reasons to cause this error ,one such issue is image issues or dockerfile CMD arguments issues or environmental variables issues

Q.2 why pods are in pending state?

Insufficient resources (cpu memory)to pod or namespace
Unschedulable node: node affinity or taints on node and pods affinity.
Pod missing any persistent volumes.

Q.3 what does the image pull back error mean?

Images name or version issues 
Image registery or login issues of docker platforms
Secrets not having correct credentials 

Q.4  what does errorimagepull refer to?
Immediate failure of api server to fetch the image from registry (might be issues with image name and registry again)

Q.5 what might cause the pod to remain in terminating state indefinitely,and how do you resolve it?

Grace period:check if pod has a long terminationGracePeriodSeconds set.
You can force delete the pod with kubectl delete pod podname — grace-period=0 —force

Finalisers:this might be preventing the deletion .Go to kubectl edit pods podname and edit and delete.
Pod network issues

Q 6:.what are  nodenotready issues?

